title The ceiling frozen before the product existed
prompt autonomous lap -- pheromone, the Glow product language seam
rota lap 5046, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; advanced by hand past row 1, which the three laps before me all read. Fire's instruction is to read the ledger before reading anything new and to look straight at the bright point -- which sent me at my own ladder rung rather than at a new idea.
think My rung reads express the receipt facts in the smallest Glow form already owned. So I went to write the shape, and counted the fields first.
think The contract's ReceiptOfferFact names fifteen. glow/rune_shape.rye declares max_fields: u32 = 9, and that line carries no comment at all -- alone among the bounds around it, in a tree whose own law asks every named constant to say why.
think Before assuming it was an oversight I looked for the reason, and found one: a seated capacity freeze of 20260720, recorded in context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md and argued in its own brief. So the widening is Keaton's word and this lap widens nothing.
think Two earlier candidates died by measurement, which is the lap's real economy. A rune/lower/witness naming grid showed four holes and all four are covered under other names. Three declared error members reachable from nowhere are already counted by tools/fixtures/e/error_member_reach_scan.sh, built five days ago -- the absence law's exact warning, met by grepping before building.
obs THE FREEZE'S REASON WAS TRUE AND IS NOW SPENT. It stopped the ladder at nona because another face name teaches no new nest law -- true while the rungs were copy-paste Greek numerals, pair through nona, and nothing asked for a tenth. The accepted contract asks now, with a requirement rather than a preference, and the freeze names its own escape in the same breath.
obs ALL FIFTEEN FIELDS FIT AN AURA GLOW ALREADY ADMITS, so the capacity is the only thing in the way. value_amount needs @u64 because the contract's 9,000,000,000 ceiling stands above what @u32 holds; product_digest fits @ux at exactly its 32 bytes. That half was read by hand, and the scan says so in its own header, because the contract names field names rather than types and no reader can derive it.
obs THE GATE IS THE INSTRUMENT, NEVER THE GAP. A reader that silently parses zero types prints a flawless types_over_capacity=0 about a page it never opened, so both halves read and at least one type parsed are gated. The gap is reported: closing it is a ruling no lap may take, and a gate that reds every ship for that is a gate somebody turns off -- the published-double shape one law over.
obs MY OWN PEN CAUGHT MY OWN SCAN before it shipped. The first draft split a field line on commas before trimming the colon, so offer: map<a, b> read as two fields. A line carrying a colon is one field now, and both directions are legs.
obs A REBASE RESURRECTED TWO CLOSED CLAIMS. 85a8684c1 replayed a stale construction/fleet-claims.kyri over my close at 24cd44150, so four landed claims -- my two, bakery's and diffuser's -- stood status=building on the board every ship opens. The six-hour expiry bounds it; a board half stale for hours is the cost, and mine are closed again in this send.
obs THE COLD ENDURANCE RUN READS tree_moved=yes, honestly and by my hand. It read 131 guards on the inherited tree before I published the claim the baton asks for before a build, and exactly one of those was red. The authoritative reading is the hot endurance run on a settled tree.
